{
 "manufacturer": "ABB",
 "manufacturer_slug": "abb",
 "model": "ACS310 pump and fan drive (embedded Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "acs310",
 "short_model": "ACS310",
 "aliases": [
  "ACS310-01E",
  "ACS310-01U",
  "ACS310-03E",
  "ACS310-03U"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "ACS310 drives (01E/01U/03E/03U) using the embedded fieldbus: Modbus RTU on the built-in EIA-485 terminals 23-26 or RS-232 on the panel connector; user's manual 3AUA0000044201 Rev D.",
 "summary": "ABB's ACS310 is a compact drive for pumps and fans with Modbus RTU built in on its I/O terminals. Every value is a 16-bit holding register: 40001-40006 carry the ABB Drives control word, two references, status word and two selectable actual values, 40031-40034 the DCU profile words, and each parameter NNNN sits at register 4NNNN. This map covers the control block, the main actual signals, fault and alarm words, fault history and the communication set-up parameters.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The manual lists 4xxxx holding registers and states that register 4xxxx is sent as xxxx - 1 in the Modbus message (its example: 40002 is addressed as 0001), so 40001 = wire address 0. Parameter NNNN sits at register 4NNNN (e.g. 0103 -> 40103, wire 102; 3018 -> 43018, wire 3017)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "ACS310 drives user's manual",
  "doc_number": "3AUA0000044201 Rev D",
  "revision_date": "2016-01-11",
  "url": "https://search.abb.com/library/Download.aspx?DocumentID=3AUA0000044201&LanguageCode=en&DocumentPartId=1&Action=Launch",
  "pages": "FbEq definition p. 164; groups 01/03/04 pp. 170-176; 1607 p. 195; 3018/3019 p. 217; group 53 pp. 259-261; 9802 p. 261; embedded fieldbus chapter pp. 287-310 (setup p. 289, drive control parameters pp. 291-292, reference scaling p. 296, function codes p. 298, register mapping pp. 299-301 incl. 'xxxx - 1' rule, exception codes p. 301, ABB Drives CW/SW pp. 302-305)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "There are no 32-bit registers: the manual states all values read or written are limited to 16 bits (-32768...32767). Signals that can be negative are listed as INT16.",
  "Scaling is the manual's FbEq column (fieldbus integer per unit, e.g. '1 = 0.1 Hz' -> scale 0.1).",
  "40001 and 40004 work only with 5305 = ABB DRV LIM or ABB DRV FULL; 40031-40034 only with 5305 = DCU PROFILE. Control word bits 4 and 10 work only with ABB DRV FULL.",
  "Actual values 40005-40012 follow 5310-5317 (all default 0 in the parameter list). Their scaling is that of the chosen signal, so they are left unscaled; 40007-40012 are not listed.",
  "Reference scaling (ABB Drives profile): REF1 20000 = 1105 REF1 MAX, REF2 10000 = 1108 REF2 MAX; final references are limited by 1104/1105 and 1107/1108.",
  "Group 03 fault and alarm words are listed read-only, but the manual says an alarm can be cleared by writing zero to the whole alarm word.",
  "Left out: analog I/O, PID and process-variable signals (0116-0139, units depend on configuration), 0402/0403 fault time stamps, 0409 status at fault, energy-saving counters, 40080-40089 Modbus data OUT, and all motor/application parameters.",
  "Coils (control-word bits 1-16, relay outputs from 33), discrete inputs and two input registers (analog inputs) are mentioned in the function code table but not listed here."
 ],
